      ],
      "solution": "$3\\log_9 2 - \\log_9 24 = 3\\log_9 2 - \\log_9(8 \\times 3) = 3\\log_9 2 - \\log_9(2^3 \\times 9^{\\frac{1}{2}}) = 3\\log_9 2 - (\\log_9(2^3) + \\log_9(9^{\\frac{1}{2}})) = 3\\log_9 2 - (3\\log_9 2 + \\frac{1}{2}) = -\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Combine terms using log quotient rule: $k\\log_b x = \\log_b(x^k)$ and $\\log_b u - \\log_b v = \\log_b(u/v)$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Rewrite $3\\log_9 2$ as $\\log_9(2^3) = \\log_9 8$.",
          "Combine: $\\log_9 8 - \\log_9 24 = \\log_9\\left(\\frac{8}{24}\\right) = \\log_9\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)$.",
          "Express $\\frac{1}{3} = 3^{-1} = (9^{1/2})^{-1} = 9^{-1/2}$.",
          "Evaluate $\\log_9(9^{-1/2}) = -\\frac{1}{2}$."
